When uc_vm_call() invoked a native function, it inspected the type of
the function value after the call returned. The frame of the native
callee released the function value on return, so if the stack slot
held the only other reference, the type check read freed memory.

`render()` calls the function in its first argument slot through
uc_vm_call(). The function value below has no reference other than
that slot, because its module is removed from the modules table
before the call.

This test depends on running under a memory checker.

-- Testcase --
function access_fn_get() {
	let fs = require('fs');

	delete modules.fs;

	return fs.access;
}

print(length(render(access_fn_get(), '/')), "\n");
-- End --

-- Args --
-R
-- End --

